## Anatomy

| Region | Components | Role |
|---|---|---|
| Navigation | [TxTabs / TxTabItemGroup / TxTabItem](/docs/dev/components/tabs) | Grouped section navigation; `name` is a stable English key and the localised label goes in the `#name` slot; a block indicator slides to the current section |
| Header | TxTabHeader from [TxTabs](/docs/dev/components/tabs), [TxStatusBadge](/docs/dev/components/status-badge), [TxButton](/docs/dev/components/button) | Section title, autosave status, the Reset entry |
| Setting rows | [TxGroupBlock / TxBlockSlot / TxBlockLine](/docs/dev/components/group-block) | Groups of 56px setting rows; the groups stay open |
| General and CoreBox | [TuffSwitch](/docs/dev/components/switch), [TxFlatSelect](/docs/dev/components/flat-select), [TxFlatRadio](/docs/dev/components/flat-radio), [TxSlider](/docs/dev/components/slider), [TxSelect](/docs/dev/components/select), [TxSegmentedSlider](/docs/dev/components/segmented-slider), [TxNumberInput](/docs/dev/components/number-input), [TxInput](/docs/dev/components/input), [TxKbd](/docs/dev/components/kbd) | Language, theme, opacity, launch at login, a recordable summon shortcut, auto paste, result density, max results, placeholder text |
| Shortcuts | [TxSearchInput](/docs/dev/components/search-input), [TxKbd](/docs/dev/components/kbd), [TuffSwitch](/docs/dev/components/switch), [TxSearchEmpty](/docs/dev/components/search-empty) | A filterable list of global shortcuts, each with its own switch; the owning plugin is named in the description |
| AI and privacy | [TxAlert](/docs/dev/components/alert), [TxSensitiveInput](/docs/dev/components/sensitive-input), [TxCheckbox](/docs/dev/components/checkbox), [TxRadioGroup / TxRadio](/docs/dev/components/radio) | How Nexus routes requests, provider and temperature, your own key, readable context, clipboard retention, excluded apps |
| Account | [TxAvatar](/docs/dev/components/avatar), [TxImageUploader](/docs/dev/components/image-uploader) | Avatar upload, display name, email and plan |
| Confirmations | [TxModal](/docs/dev/components/modal), [TxCheckbox](/docs/dev/components/checkbox) | Reset all settings, clear clipboard history (optionally with pinned items), sign out of other devices |
| Live preview (wide) | [TxIconChip](/docs/dev/components/icon-chip), a hand-built miniature CoreBox | Theme, opacity, result density, max results, placeholder text and the summon shortcut, live |

## Interactions

- Change anything and the header shows Saving…, then Saved · just now once 600 ms pass without another change.
- The summon shortcut can be recorded: press Record, then a combination that includes ⌘, ⌃ or ⌥; Esc or clicking away cancels. The Open CoreBox row on the Shortcuts page shows the new combination too.
- The Shortcuts page can be filtered and each shortcut switched off. The API key on AI models is masked until clicked, and copying it writes to your real clipboard (it is a sample value, not a real key).
- Reset, clearing clipboard history and signing out of other devices all confirm first; after a clear, the Privacy page reports the result and the record count updates.
- Once in view it plays once: at 1 s it moves to CoreBox, at 1.6 s it changes result density from Cozy to Compact and the header runs through its save states, while the wide preview turns compact alongside. Any interaction stops it; with reduced motion on, the final state shows straight away and the tab-switch animation is turned off.
- Wide (≥ 960px) adds the live preview on the right; narrow (< 640px) moves the navigation into a row across the top, drops the group headings and puts each row's control under its label.

## Adapting it

- Real storage: replace the timer in `watch(settings)` with a debounced write (a local config file or Nexus sync), and on failure set the status to Not saved with a retry.
- Adding a section: add a TxTabItem to the right TxTabItemGroup with a stable English `name` and the label in the `#name` slot — using the visible label as `name` loses the current section when the interface language changes. TxTabs unmounts panels you leave, so keep values out of the row components; hold your own object URL for an avatar too, because TxImageUploader revokes the URLs it created when it unmounts.
- Keep TxGroupBlock at `collapsible=false`: its expand and collapse are driven by gsap with no reduced-motion fallback. Do not set `memoryName` either, or it writes to localStorage.
- Put sensitive fields in a group's body rather than a 56px row: TxSensitiveInput's copy tab floats above the field and would overlap the row before it. TxFlatSelect opens in place without teleporting, so place it where no scroll container clips it and raise its row's stacking level (every setting row is its own stacking context).
